reen\n│\n│\n│                     title.txt                   Home\n│\n│                                  M records parents C and B.\n│"},{"step":"countercase","title":"Answer: no. Without C, main just moves to B","line":"A is in B’s history, so moving main to B loses nothing.","caption":"Here main never made C and still points at A, B’s parent. git merge feature moves main to B without a new commit, which Git calls a fast-forward, and colour.txt turns green. Git fast-forwards by default; the option --no-ff would make a merge commit here anyway, by choice, though no edit would be lost without one.","start":62.267,"end":83.267,"hold":62.967,"state":{"frame":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null}],"main":"B","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"B","merge":"fast-forward"},"files":{"colour":"green","title":null},"advanced":false},"changed":{"frame":{"before":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"},{"id":"M","parents":["C","B"],"colour":"green","title":"Home"}],"main":"M","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"M","merge":"commit"},"after":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null}],"main":"B","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"B","merge":"fast-forward"}},"files":{"before":{"colour":"green","title":"Home"},"after":{"colour":"green","title":null}},"advanced":{"before":true,"after":false}},"picture":"A. B. feature. main. HEAD. File. Working contents. colour.txt. green. title.txt. absent. main moves to existing commit B.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                                   ┌────────────────┐┌────────────┐\n│                                   │    feature     ││   main     ◀────   HEAD\n│                                   └────────────────┘└────────────┘\n│                                               ╭─────╮\n│                                         ───────  B  │\n│             ╭─────╮       ──────────────      │     │\n│             │  A  │◀──────                    ╰─────╯\n│             │     │\n│             ╰─────╯\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                    File                             Working contents\n│                   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│                      colour.txt                green\n│\n│\n│                     title.txt                  absent\n│\n│                               main moves to existing commit B.\n│"}]},{"values":{"history":"linear"},"name":"Main history: Main stays at the shared commit","duration":63.033,"paper":"#ffffff","steps":[{"step":"question","title":"Only feature moved on. Can a merge just move main to B?","line":"Predict: if the main label moved to B, would main lose anything?","caption":"Both branches started at A, where colour.txt is blue. On feature, B made it green; main has made no commit since, so it still points at A. We have main checked out (HEAD), so the files below are A’s. A branch label names a commit; arrows lead back through its history. Could moving main to B bring in feature’s edit?","start":0,"end":22.5,"hold":0.533,"state":{"frame":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null}],"main":"A","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"A","merge":"none"},"files":{"colour":"blue","title":null},"advanced":false},"changed":{"frame":{"after":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null}],"main":"A","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"A","merge":"none"}},"files":{"after":{"colour":"blue","title":null}},"advanced":{"after":false}},"picture":"A. B. feature. main. HEAD. File. Working contents. co